From e1c49a7cb78aaf305b7ee1c5b82f00641279270f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini experiment archive <experiment@invalid.example>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 18:40:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] pstore: fail native initialization when old log allocation
 fails

A valid nonempty retained ring must have an old-log copy before
initialization succeeds. Otherwise ramoops_init_prz() clears the
current metadata despite failure to preserve the old record. Return
ENOMEM so persistent_ram_new() unmaps and reports failure before
the ramoops caller reaches its zap.

This native 3.18 experiment prerequisite is tested with exact function
bodies and injected allocation failure. ECC is disabled in the fixture;
no physical persistence or full kernel build is established.
The archive identity is synthetic and non-certifying; not submission-ready.
---
 fs/pstore/ram_core.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fs/pstore/ram_core.c b/fs/pstore/ram_core.c
index e964eee..7ab712d 100644
--- a/fs/pstore/ram_core.c
+++ b/fs/pstore/ram_core.c
@@ -494,6 +494,8 @@ static int persistent_ram_post_init(struct persistent_ram_zone *prz, u32 sig,
 			pr_debug("found existing buffer, size %zu, start %zu\n",
 				 buffer_size(prz), buffer_start(prz));
 			persistent_ram_save_old(prz);
+			if (buffer_size(prz) && !prz->old_log)
+				return -ENOMEM;
 			return 0;
 		}
 	} else {
